\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rationale given: 
\f0\b First-In-Last-Out (like a stack)
\f1\b0  \'97 whichever middleware "opened" first (e.g., opened a DB connection) should be the last to "close." (Contrasted explicitly with FIFO/queue behavior.)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl0
\f3\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 wrap_tool_call
\f1\fs24  order is 
\f0\b not
\f1\b0  reversed \'97 it follows the same declared order as the others (MW1 
\f6 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  MW2 
\f6 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  MW3), unlike the after-hooks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.6 Best practices (from docs, lightly covered)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls23\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Keep each middleware focused on one responsibility.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Handle errors gracefully \'97 don't let middleware itself crash the agent.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Choose the right hook type (node-style vs wrap-style) for the job.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Document any custom state fields clearly.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Unit-test middleware independently.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Be conscious of execution order when stacking multiple middlewares.\
\ls23\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prefer built-in middleware over writing custom versions whenever one already covers the need.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
