\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 4. Key Recurring Themes / Instructor Emphasis\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls24\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 "Code over LLM judgment" principle:
\f1\b0  wherever a decision can be made deterministically in code (e.g., filtering tools by login state, validating an ID format), do it in code \'97 don't rely on the LLM to "remember" instructions, because LLMs are fuzzy/non-deterministic and code is not.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls24\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Middleware/hooks/callbacks are 
\f0\b the same underlying concept across frameworks
\f1\b0  (LangChain, Google ADK, Claude Code) \'97 different vocabulary, same mechanism of intercepting an agent's execution lifecycle.\
\ls24\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Debugging mindset stressed repeatedly: read official documentation and API references over relying on tutorials/YouTube, since docs are the ground truth.\
\ls24\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f0\b Shell Tool Middleware
